er@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-28T20:36:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-29T10:11:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-29T10:11:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-29T10:11:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-29T22:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-31T13:00:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Indianapolis IN","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 29 at 10:11AM CDT until August 31 at 1:00PM CDT by NWS Indianapolis IN","description":"...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nIllinois...Indiana...\n\nWabash River at Vincennes\n\n...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in\nIllinois...Indiana...\n\nWabash River at Hutsonville Legacy Power Plant Site\n\nWabash River at Riverton\n\n.Minor flooding continues on the Wabash River from Hutsonville down\nto Vincennes. The river has crested. Flooding should come to an end\non the Wabash over the weekend.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Wabash River at Riverton.\n\n* WHEN...Until Monday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 18.0 feet, Extensive lowland flooding is in progress.\nHigh water surrounds many river cabins.  Access to most river\ncabins is by boat only.  Levees begin to protect farmland.\nExtensive flooding of Leaverton Park occurs in Palestine, Illinois.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 10:00 AM CDT /11:00 AM EDT/ Saturday the stage was 18.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 10.5 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 10:00 AM CDT /11:00 AM EDT/ Saturday was 19.4 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage early\nMonday morning and continue falling to 5.1 feet Tuesday,\nSeptember 08.\n- Flood stage is 15.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/ind.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 1015 PM CDT /1115\nPM EDT/.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSIND"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS83 KIND 291511"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL MONDAY AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KIND.FL.W.0162.000000T0000Z-260831T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-31T13:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d6d2ad6897bfc2053b7ba54c44a8a9b438cb92a.002.1,2026-08-28T09:43:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd9499db912cf41eedf6e7ed89ab331259907008.004.1,2026-08-27T20:38:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6315cb2dc8d0f54eaa778ad01fb00cd0c181d340.003.1,2026-08-27T10:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.370c270d7d1b162addcf02dc7258854c454ad061.003.1,2026-08-26T13:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.12919d77a71ad3fa4d2d46fe4c889e8395a827c1.005.1,2026-08-26T09:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.21fed40f8a4270468743863bc5d2282950a3b72d.006.1,2026-08-25T13:12:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.966efdc66b3086f5aa2b21cb1cfbfa88e06cea31.007.1,2026-08-25T08:35:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.485716edaea873f78d95b8660a4bf26eec3149e1.008.1,2026-08-24T12:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d17042b1f0925f697c4f2f6f4a97ea6a0fc7af62.006.1,2026-08-24T20:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e611d888f0b860bf842f3076e8bd792348b6b8d0.008.1,2026-08-24T08:54:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.946a70c1dd6536458e250ec5f6d5adee0ba9c93c.002.1,2026-08-23T21:48:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.80aefc3a77c6080a84755a24ef28fd6d4a72367f.