s.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 29 at 2:42PM EDT until August 29 at 3:15PM EDT by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL","description":"SVRTBW\n\nThe National Weather Service in Ruskin has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nSouth central Lee County in southwestern Florida...\n\n* Until 315 PM EDT.\n\n* At 242 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Lovers Key\nState Park, or over Bonita Beach, moving west at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nBonita Springs, Fort Myers Beach, Lovers Key State Park, Estero,\nBonita Beach, Punta Rassa, San Carlos Park, and Three Oaks.","instruction":"For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a\nbuilding.","response":"Shelter","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SVRTBW"],"WMOidentifier":["WUUS52 KTBW 291842"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-29T18:42:00-00:00...storm...112DEG...12KT...26.38,-81.86"],"windThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxWindGust":["60 MPH"],"hailThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxHailSize":["Up to .75"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KTBW.SV.W.0037.260829T1842Z-260829T1915Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-29T15:15:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SVR"],"NationalWeatherService":["SVW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.75a06b0b8c574078d7da161ad4d67431c7ed4458.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-78.15,34.92],[-78.24,34.91],[-78.41,34.94],[-78.47,35.06],[-78.38,35.17],[-78.27,35.23],[-78.19,35.21],[-78.16,35.19],[-78.16,35.14],[-78.17,35.12],[-78.17,35.09],[-78.16,35.08],[-78.16,35.04],[-78.15,34.92]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.75a06b0b8c574078d7da161ad4d67431c7ed4458.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.75a06b0b8c574078d7da161ad4d67431c7ed4458.001.1","areaDesc":"Sampson, NC","geocode":{"SAME":["037163"],"UGC":["NCC163"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/NCC163"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-29T14:25:00-04:00","effective":"2026-08-29T14:25:00-04:00","onset":"2026-08-29T14:25:00-04:00","expires":"2026-08-29T17:30:00-04:00","ends":"2026-08-29T17:30:00-04:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flash Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Raleigh NC","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 29 at 2:25PM EDT until August 29 at 5:30PM EDT by NWS Raleigh NC","description":"FFWRAH\n\nThe National Weather Service in Raleigh has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNortheastern Sampson County in central North Carolina...\n\n* Until 530 PM EDT.\n\n* At 225 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 2 and 3 inches of rain\nhave fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nClinton, Turkey and Hobbton.","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FFWRAH"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS52 KRAH 291825"],"flashFloodDetection":["RADAR INDICATED"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KRAH.FF.W.0037.260829T1825Z-260829T2130Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-29T17:30:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FFW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FFW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.94bbd3bf7d5c64c7a9eaa4782fba08f6d22c291f.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-107.18,41.64],[-107.36,41.82],[-106.69,42.16],[-106.49,41.92],[-107.18,41.64]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.94bbd3bf7d5c64c7a9eaa4782fba08f6d22c291f.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.94bbd3bf7d5c64c7a9eaa4782fba08f6d22c291f.001.1","areaDesc":"Carbon, WY","geocode":{"SAME":["056007"],"UGC":["WYC007"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/WYC007"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-29T12:51:00-06:00","effective":"2026-08-29T12:51:00-06:00","onset":"2026-08-29T12:51:00-06:00","expires":"2026-08-29T13:30:00-06:00","ends":"2026-08-29T13:30:00-06:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Cheyenne WY","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 29 at 12:51PM MDT until August 29 at 1:30PM MDT by NWS Cheyenne WY","description":"SVRCYS\n\nThe National Weather Service in Cheyenne has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nCentral Carbon County in south central Wyoming...\n\n* Until 130 PM MDT.\n\n* At 1250 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Sinclair, or\nnear Rawlins, moving northeast at 50 mph.\n\nHAZARD...70 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Automated sensors.\n\nIMPACT...Expect considerable tree damage. Damage is likely to\nmobile homes, roofs, and outbuildings.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nRawlins, Sinclair, Fort Steele Historic Site, Rawlins Municipal\nAirport, Dugway Campground, Seminoe State Park, and Carbon County\nFairgrounds.","instruction":"For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a\nbuilding.","response":"Shelter","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SVRCYS"],"WMOidentifier":["WUUS55 KCYS 291851"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-29T18:50:00-00:00...storm...239DEG...44KT...41.8,-107.14"],"windThreat":["OBSERVED"],"maxWindGust":["70 MPH"],"hailThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxHailSize":["Up to .75"],"thunderstormDamageThreat":["CONSIDERABLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KCYS.SV.W.0315.260829T1851Z-260829T1930Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-29T13:30:00-06:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SVR"],"NationalWeatherService":["SVW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a136c271a9da236574d34f5291932d9471483ce6.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-119.02,48.1],[-119.01,48.04],[-118.96,48.02],[-118.99,47.95],[-118.93,47.94],[-118.84,47.96],[-118.83,47.94],[-119.2,47.72],[-119.35,47.84],[-119.04,48.11],[-119.02,48.1]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a136c271a9da236574d34f5291932d9471483ce6.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a136c271a9da236574d34f5291932d9471483ce6.001.1","areaDesc":"Douglas, WA; Grant, WA; Lincoln, WA","geocode":{"SAME":["053017","053025","053043"],"UGC":["WAC017","WAC025","WAC043"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/WAC017","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/WAC025","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/WAC043"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-29T11:51:00-07:00","effective":"2026-08-29T11:51:00-07:00","onset":"2026-08-29T11:51:00-07:00","expires":"2026-08-29T12:30:00-07:00","ends":"2026-08-29T12:30:00-07:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Spokane WA","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 29 at 11:51AM PDT until August 29 at 12:30PM PDT by NWS Spokane WA","description":"SVROTX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Spokane has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nEastern Douglas County in north central Washington...\nNorthwestern Lincoln County in eastern Washington...\nNortheastern Grant County in north central Washington...\n\n* Until 1230 PM PDT.\n\n* At 1150 AM PDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 17 miles south of\nNespelem Community, or 38 miles southeast of Omak, moving northeast\nat 35 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nCoulee Dam, Grand Coulee, Electric City, and Spring Canyon\nCampground.","instruction":"Remain alert for a possible tornado! Tornadoes can develop quickly\nfrom severe thunderstorms. If you spot a tornado go at once into the\nbasement or small central room in a sturdy structure.\n\nFor your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a\nbuilding.","response":"Shelter","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SVROTX"],"WMOidentifier":["WUUS56 KOTX 291851"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-29T18:50:00-00:00...storm...230DEG...28KT...47.94,-119.13"],"windThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxWindGust":["60 MPH"],"hailThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxHailSize":["Up to .75"],"tornadoDetection":["POSSIBLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KOTX.SV.W.0029.260829T1851Z-260829T1930Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-29T12:30:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SVR"],"NationalWeatherService":["SVW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c69acc99453eb262296380cfce9671cd00218627.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-81.84,26.33],[-82.16,26.22],[-82.17,26.23],[-82.34,26.53],[-82,26.66],[-82.01,26.59],[-81.94,26.53],[-81.84,26.53],[-81.84,26.52],[-81.83,26.5],[-81.84,26.33]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c69acc99453eb262296380cfce9671cd00218627.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c69acc99453eb262296380cfce9671cd00218627.001.1","areaDesc":"Charlotte Harbor and Pine Island Sound; Coastal waters from Bonita Beach to Englewood FL out 20 NM","geocode":{"SAME":["077836","077856"],"UGC":["GMZ836","GMZ856"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/GMZ836","https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/GMZ856"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8c1cc13d0c808d1872c060551ad91754cbb208ae.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8c1cc13d0c808d1872c060551ad91754cbb208ae.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-29T14:25:00-04:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-29T14:45:00-04:00","effective":"2026-08-29T14:45:00-04:00","onset":"2026-08-29T14:45:00-04:00","expires":"2026-08-29T15:30:00-04:00","ends":"2026-08-29T15:30:00-04:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Special Marine Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL","headline":"Special Marine Warning issued August 29 at 2:45PM EDT until August 29 at 3:30PM EDT by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL","description":"For the following areas...\nCharlotte Harbor and Pine Island Sound...\nCoastal waters from Bonita Beach to Englewood FL out 20 NM...\n\nAt 245 PM EDT, strong thunderstorms were located along a line\nextending from 22 nm northeast of Fort Myers Beach to 6 nm northeast\nof Lovers Key State Park to 10 nm west of Naples, moving west at 5\nknots.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts to nearly 50 knots.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, suddenly higher\nwaves, frequent lightning, and heavy downpours. Make sure\nall on board are wearing life jackets.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nLovers Key State Park, Captiva, Sanibel, Fort Myers Beach, Bonita\nBeach, and North Captiva Island.","instruction":"Move to safe harbor immediately as gusty winds and high waves are\nexpected.\n\nFrequent lightning is occurring with these storms. If caught on the\nopen water stay below deck if possible, keep away from ungrounded\nmetal objects.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["MWSTBW"],"WMOidentifier":["FZUS72 KTBW 291845"],"NWSheadline":["A SPECIAL MARINE WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 330 PM EDT"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-29T18:45:00-00:00...storm...103DEG...7KT...26.7,-81.63 26.49,-81.79 26.15,-81.98"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KTBW.MA.W.0168.000000T0000Z-260829T1930Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-29T15:30:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["NWS"],"NationalWeatherService":["MAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1be4c9277f4134b8569b02d7fae8f567ba81212.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-112.84,34.32],[-113.04,34.4],[-112.97,34.64],[-112.66,34.56],[-112.84,34.32]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1be4c9277f4134b8569b02d7fae8f567ba81212.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1be4c9277f4134b8569b02d7fae8f567ba81212.001.1","areaDesc":"Yavapai, AZ","geocode":{"SAME":["004025"],"UGC":["AZC025"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/AZC025"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-29T11:52:00-07:00","effective":"2026-08-29T11:52:00-07:00","onset":"2026-08-29T11:52:00-07:00","expires":"2026-08-29T12:15:00-07:00","ends":"2026-08-29T12:15:00-07:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Flagstaff AZ","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 29 at 11:52AM MST until August 29 at 12:15PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ","description":"SVRFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nYavapai County in west central Arizona...\n\n* Until 1215 PM MST.\n\n* At 1152 AM MST, a severe thunderstorm was located near Yava in\nrural areas of Yavapai County, moving north at 25 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to\nroofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nYava and rural areas of Yavapai County.\n\nThis includes State Route 96 between mile markers 14 and 21.","instruction":"Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from\nwindows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds and large\nhail.\n\nTorrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to\nflash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.","response":"Shelter","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SVRFGZ"],"WMOidentifier":["WUUS55 KFGZ 291852"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-29T18:50:00-00:00...storm...201DEG...21KT...34.4,-112.92"],"windThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxWindGust":["60 MPH"],"hailThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxHailSize":["1.00"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KFGZ.SV.W.0101.260829T1852Z-260829T1915Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-29T12:15:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SVR"],"NationalWeatherService":["SVW"]}}}]}